<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<plist version="1.0">
<!--
  Hardened-runtime entitlements for the signed app (#228, ADR 013). Only one key, with its reason:
  - com.apple.security.personal-information.calendars: the resource entitlement of the hardened runtime that covers
    EventKit, Reminders included (there is no separate Reminders key). Without it a notarized build cannot show the
    Reminders prompt or read a reminder (#550, ADR 022, epic #481).
  Why nothing else is needed:
  - WKWebView runs JavaScript (and its JIT) in Apple-signed WebContent processes, so the app itself
    needs no com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit.
  - Tokens use the legacy login Keychain through the Security framework, which needs no entitlement.
  - The app is not sandboxed, so network and file access need none either.
  - It loads no third-party plug-ins or unsigned dylibs, so library validation stays on.
  Add a key only when a notarized build or its runtime logs prove it is needed, with the reason here.
-->
<dict>
  <key>com.apple.security.personal-information.calendars</key>
  <true/>
</dict>
</plist>
